# gayle: its .moddata keys (amix-dlm C3-1 section 3, C4-2 section 1) and the
# definition line, as the ABI kit's mkmod reads a Master.  One Master for both
# lines: no $cpu, the kit's fragment gives the line's (68030 on k30, 68040 on
# k46); kabi and cc come from the kit.
# $class root: loaded by the core's root pass before the root is mounted; a
# root-class module is never unloaded ($unload never).
# $match mobo:gayle: the registered motherboard probe; gayle_load's own gated
# probe decides (VPOSR AGA gate, bprobe of ALTSTAT, task-file readback).
# $rank ide: sd's class 4 (C4-1 section 4), the argument gayle_load passes to
# sd_register.  No $majors: sd owns the disk majors.
# $modtype misc: MOD_HDRV_WRAPPER, no switch-table slot.
# Parameters (the static driver's per-kernel tunables): intr 1 = attach INT2
# after the self-test (default polled); slave 0 never touch the slave, 1 any
# drive, 2 ATAPI only; debug 0..2; master/slaveunit the SCSI unit numbers.
$modtype misc
$class root
$match mobo:gayle
$rank ide
$unload never
$param intr:int:0:0:1
$param slave:int:0:0:2
$param debug:int:0:0:2
$param master:int:6:0:7
$param slaveunit:int:5:0:7
$desc A4000 Gayle IDE, root-class disk controller
gayle	gayle
